# chezmoi ignore rules (this file is itself templated).
#
# The home-lab admin kubeconfig (~/.kube/homelab.yaml) is a cluster-admin
# credential. Deploy it ONLY on personal, non-server devices — never work
# machines (profile != "personal"), and not on the cluster nodes themselves
# (machine == "server", which already have /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml). Also
# never during an automated container-image build — those images publish
# publicly, so `chezmoi apply` there must never fetch a live secret no
# matter which .profile/.machine values the build happens to pass. Image
# builds set DOTFILES_IMAGE_BUILD (any non-empty value) before running
# `chezmoi apply`; see homelab-dev-templates images/base/DOTFILES-AUDIT.md.
# The matching KUBECONFIG export in dot_config/shell/exports.zsh.tmpl uses
# the profile/machine half of this gate. See homelab #132.
# The gate is positive: these deploy only where a Bitwarden vault is
# actually configured, because the kubeconfig template calls `bitwarden`
# specifically -- secrets = "1password" fails exactly as "none" does.
# Ephemeral machines are excluded unless their template opts in by setting
# WORKSPACE_CLUSTER_ADMIN, which confines cluster-admin to one designated
# template rather than every workspace. The assignments deliberately carry
# no left-trim marker: one there swallows the newline ending this comment
# and emits the first path onto the comment line, silently un-ignoring it.
{{ $vault := or (eq .secrets "bitwarden") (eq .secrets "both") -}}
{{ $trusted := or (and (eq .profile "personal") (ne .machine "server") (ne .machine "ephemeral")) (env "WORKSPACE_CLUSTER_ADMIN") -}}
{{ if not (and $vault $trusted) -}}
.kube/homelab.yaml
.local/bin/mcp-breakglass
{{ end -}}

# ─── Home-directory audit (dotfiles #28) ──────────────────────────────────
# Record of unmanaged files deliberately kept OUT of management, so the
# decision is explicit. Most live only on the machine that needs them.
#
# Secrets / credentials — NEVER track in plaintext. If one ever needs to
# reproduce across machines, template it via Bitwarden (see .kube above).
# (.config/gh/hosts.yml is the secret sibling of the tracked gh/config.yml;
# it holds the GitHub host/user identity, and off macOS the OAuth token.)
.config/gh/hosts.yml
.config/rclone/rclone.conf
.simplefin_access_url
.simplefin_token
.pi/agent/auth.json
.terraform.d/credentials.tfrc.json
.claude.json
#
# Claude Code machine-local state / caches. Portable Claude config lives in
# dot_claude/ (settings.json.tmpl, CLAUDE.md, agents/, commands/, skills/,
# hooks/); the entries below are per-machine state, never tracked — so a broad
# `chezmoi add` (e.g. from /chezmoi-sync) can't capture them.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/daemon.status.json
.claude/mcp-needs-auth-cache.json
.claude/stats-cache.json
.claude/.distill-watermark
.claude/hooks/__pycache__/
#
# Intentional non-secret excludes (stock defaults, machine state, or obsolete):
#   .bashrc / .profile          stock Ubuntu + machine-local conda init
#   .hyper.js / .config/tabby    obsolete — migrated to ghostty (managed)
#   .config/Vial/Vial.conf       window-geometry state only; pending homelab #179
#   .config/monitors.xml         machine-specific display layout
#   .config/QtProject.conf       Qt file-dialog state, not config
#   .config/user-dirs.dirs       stock XDG defaults
#   .config/xclicker.conf        low-value app state
#   .yarnrc                      autogenerated update-check timestamp
#   .pi/agent/settings.json      .pi agent tool — excluded entirely
#   browsers / Signal / Proton / caches / toolchain dirs   not portable config
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
